# PostgreSQL Performance Profiles for FraiseQL Benchmarks
#
# This file documents the available hardware profiles for benchmarking.
# Select a profile by copying it to .env before running docker-compose.
#
# Usage:
#   cp .env.laptop .env              # For laptop development
#   cp .env.standard .env            # For medium cloud server
#   cp .env.powerful .env            # For powerful workstation (like yours: i7-13700K, 31GB RAM)
#   cp .env.ci .env                  # For CI/CD pipeline
#   docker-compose up
#
# Profiles (in order of resource availability):
# - ci:        Minimal (256MB RAM allocation) for CI/CD
# - laptop:    2GB RAM allocation (typical dev laptop)
# - standard:  8GB RAM allocation (medium cloud server, t3.large equivalent)
# - powerful:  30GB RAM allocation (powerful workstation like i7-13700K)
#
# Each profile includes:
# - shared_buffers: % of RAM dedicated to PostgreSQL cache
# - effective_cache_size: Total cache available (shared_buffers + OS cache)
# - work_mem: Per-operation sort/hash buffer
# - max_connections: Connection pool size
# - Worker processes for parallelization
#
# See individual .env.* files for exact values and comments.
